lesson: 99
title: Kilograms and grams, litres and millilitres
stars: 1
explain: One kilogram is 1000 grams, and one litre is 1000 millilitres.
explain: To share a weight or an amount of liquid into equal parts, first turn it into the small unit, then divide.
explain: 2 litres of juice is 2000 millilitres; cups of 250 millilitres hold it all in 2000 ÷ 250 = 8 cups.
vars: a=name q=2..9 s50=2..10
let: s = s50 * 50
answer: q * 1000 / s
exercise: {a} pours {q} litres of juice into cups that each hold {s} millilitres. How many cups can {a.he} fill?
exercise: {q} kilograms of flour are packed into bags of {s} grams. How many bags are there?
exercise: A jug holds {q} litres of milk. How many glasses of {s} millilitres can be filled from it?
exercise: {a} has {q} kilograms of rice and puts {s} grams into each jar. How many jars does {a.he} fill?
exercise: A bottle of {q} litres of water is shared into cups of {s} millilitres. How many cups is that?
exercise: {a} divides {q} kilograms of clay into lumps of {s} grams. How many lumps does {a.he} make?
test: How many {s}-gram packets can be made from {q} kilograms of sugar?
test: The pot has {q} litres of soup. {a} serves bowls of exactly {s} millilitres until it is empty. How many bowls does {a.he} serve?
test: A sack of potatoes weighs {q} kilograms. If every bag gets {s} grams, how many bags are filled?
test: Lemonade for the party: {q} litres. Each child gets a cup of {s} millilitres. How many children get a cup?
exercise: How many cups of {s} millilitres can {a} fill from {q} litres of juice?
exercise: {q} litres of water, cups of {s} millilitres each. How many cups?
exercise: {a} packs {q} kilograms of nuts into bags of {s} grams each. How many bags does {a.he} pack?
exercise: A farm shop in Kent has {q} kilograms of cherries and sells them in boxes of {s} grams. How many boxes can it fill?
exercise: {a} pours {q.words} litres of milk into glasses of {s} millilitres. How many glasses are filled?
exercise: There are {q} kilograms of oats. Every bowl gets {s} grams. How many bowls are there?
exercise: A tank holds {q} litres of water, and {a} fills bottles of {s} millilitres from it until it is empty. How many bottles does {a.he} fill?
exercise: {a} splits {q} kilograms of dough into rolls of {s} grams each. How many rolls does {a.he} make?
test: Into how many {s}-millilitre glasses can {q} litres of apple juice be poured?
test: A baker in Toronto weighs out {q} kilograms of flour in portions of {s} grams. How many portions does he get?
test: {s} grams per scoop and a {q}-kilogram bag of seed: how many scoops are in the bag?
test: {a} serves hot chocolate at a camp in Alberta. There are {q} litres, and every mug gets {s} millilitres. How many mugs can be served?
test: How many pots of {s} grams of honey can a beekeeper in New Zealand fill with {q} kilograms of honey?
test: {a} empties a {q}-litre jug of lemonade into cups of {s} millilitres each, with nothing left over. How many cups are filled?
exercise: {q} litres juice, cups hold {s} ml, how many cups
exercise: {q+1} kilos flour — no wait, {q} kilos, bags of {s} g. how many bags
exercise: {a} reckons {q} litres fills {q*1000/s+2} glasses of {s} ml. nah, how many glasses really
exercise: jug's got {q} litres milk, glasses {s} ml, there's 6 of us btw. how many glasses can i fill
test: how many {s}ml bottles outta {q} litres water
test: {q} kg sugar, packs of {s+50} g, sorry, {s} g. how many packs
test: {a} did {q} times {s} and got {q*s}. nah. {q} litres in {s} ml cups, how many cups really
exam: It is given that {q} litres of juice are dispensed into cups each of a capacity of {s} millilitres. Determine the number of cups which may be filled.
exam: Ascertain the number of bags, each of {s} grams, into which a quantity of {q.words} kilograms of flour may be divided without remainder.
exam: Whereas a container holds {q} litres and each glass receives {s} millilitres, state the number of glasses which can be filled therefrom.
exam: Compute the quotient of a mass of {q} kilograms divided into portions of {s} grams, expressed as the number of portions.
exercise: The café calls its cups "compact": each holds only {s} millilitres. How many cups can {a} fill from {q} litres of milk?
exercise: The late Mrs Brown left {q} kilograms of flour in her pantry. Her neighbours pack it into bags of {s} grams. How many bags do they fill?
test: bloody "fun-size" cups only hold {s} ml. {q} litres of lemonade, how many cups is that then
